  "name": "release-apogee",
  "description": "Cuts an apogee release: checks the release gate with `go run ./cmd/release status` — pushing unpushed work on main and waiting for its CI run to go green when that is all the gate lacks — drafts the notes with release-notes-apogee, proposes the version and has the owner confirm it, makes the two local release commits with `prepare`, then — after a dry run and one explicit confirmation — runs `publish`, which pushes, waits for the CI-made tag, creates the GitHub release and updates Homebrew, Scoop and winget. Optional argument vX.Y.Z proposes the version. Use for \"cut a release\", \"publish a release\", \"ship vX.Y.Z\". Only drafting the notes is release-notes-apogee.",
